<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39278" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">psaltērĭum</span></b> ,
			ĭi, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψαλτήριον</span> (e scanned short, Ven. Fort. 2, 19, 43).
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A stringed instrument of the lute kind</i>, <i>a psaltery</i>, Varr. ap.
				<i><span class="en">Non. 215, 16</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Har.
				Resp. 21, 44</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. Cir.
			178</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 1, 10, 31</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Arn. 6, 209</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Aug. in
				Psa. 32</span></i>; <i><span class="en">70</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Tert. Cor. Mil. 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. 1 Par.
				13, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Psa. 56,
			8</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a song sung to the
				psaltery.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A satire</i>, Varr. ap. <i><span class="en">Non.
				101, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Paul. Sent. 5, 4,
			16</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>The songs of David</i>, <i>the
			Psalms</i>, <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 53, 8</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">125, 11</span></i> et saep.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
